# Locales this project ships. The single declaration; scripts/check-locales.sh
# holds every other registry to it.
#
# Two columns, because the registries speak two different identifier spaces and
# conflating them is how Spanish ended up half-shipped:
#
#   store  App Store Connect locale, region-qualified: fastlane/metadata/<store>/
#          and SCREENSHOT_LANGUAGES in fastlane/Constants.rb
#   app    Xcode language, a bare subtag: knownRegions in project.pbxproj and
#          the localizations in Resources/Localizable.xcstrings
#
# "-" means "not shipped on that side". A store locale with no app language is
# a localized listing for an English build; an app language with no store
# locale is a translated build whose product page is still English -- which is
# exactly where Spanish stands until the listing lands.
#
# store   app
en-US     en
-         es
